taking a swim with gremlins could make you more compatible with monsters
but you'd probably lose too much in the deal ...

you'll want fire resistance before considering going to hell.

at your experience level the typical demon will be around level 10 with
an armor class equal to yours and they travel in packs. you are no match
for a named demon! if you get 3 more levels of experience you'll have
better control in your game!! you'll need much better armor (preferably
endowed with magic attributes).

[]Props:
[]+8 long sword named Elbereth
[]crystal plate, guantlets of power, elven boots, helm, shield, cloak
[]potion of confusion
[]I am about ready to discard mirror & bugle.  I have no idea what to
[]do with the unicorn horn.

the gauntlets of power, tinning kit and unicorn horn can all indirectly
affect the same stat, you must choose wisely ...

with the gauntlets you won't need the unicorn horn (applied tool) and
with the athame you effectively don't need the tinning kit. drop the
mirror and bugle.

you will want an AC rating < -20 (i.e. blessed scrolls of enchant armor)
and magic armor is better than generic. corrosion-proofing some of your
armor is required (but impossible if you're thinking straight, sometimes
inspiration comes after drinking to confusion and then reading scrolls,
but do not read a genocide scroll while confused!!!). a dwarvish mithril-
coat is much lighter than crystal plate and you only sacrifice 1 AC point.
dragon scale mail is far superior (and appropriately magically endowed
but this is probably a gray area for you, that is, as a wizard ask
yourself the question what could a gray dragon scale mail do that a
cloak of magic protection can't?).

a long sword named Elbereth is just a long sword. the gods have better
names for your weapons. try more sacrifices and they may reciprocate
the offer. Frost Brand or Fire Brand would be nicer, rust-proof your
long sword also.

[]I am looking for suggested items *and rationale*...

aren't we all. my advice for now: secure and improve your current
situation before considering a trip to hell. besides, nobody gets
it right the first time but they say that a wizard is more powerful
the second time around. always think contigency (i.e. can you force
a level teleport, if necessary?) ...

